# MC-E1-F2. L §2.2: period words are "the period argument of periodic and factor (day, month, quarter, year, §3.3)",
# and contextual words are reserved only in their own position; L §6.1: "A member's items mean what they mean alone".
# The member declares `index month` and writes periodic(r, month, nominal 12): there `month` is the period word, so the
# merge leaves it as written (snap9 renamed it m.month: LOAD-UNIT the period argument is a period word ... not m.month).
# The member alone and the joint model print the hole of the rate r it reads.
=== j/joint.tally
model j
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use m = "../m" sha256 "2922e2b1cf80136a61ceaab955eca198a6a6772a1cbeeded39c60b3dff306716"

ask jq: m.p law 2026-06-30
=== m/model.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

index month = month 2026-01..2026-12

input r: rate question "r?"

def p: num = periodic(r, month, nominal 12)

ask q: p law 2026-06-30
=== expect jq m.q
jq: ?"r?" (m.r)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-01-01
m.q: ?"r?" (r)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-01-01
